# Cloud-agent Linear handoff

Canonical detail: **`docs/cloud-agent-linear-handoff.md`**.

Emit a copy-paste **local-agent Linear handoff** only when this session is a Cloud Agent /
background / remote agent **and** it implemented an **already-approved plan** to completion **and**
merged that implementation PR, and Linear was not updated in-session. A local agent with Linear MCP
`ready` applies only truthful lifecycle/evidence updates on those already-approved issues. GitHub PR
linkbacks do not replace Linear.

The handoff does **not** authorize new issues, children, parents, relationships, reparenting, or scope
expansion. Newly discovered durable scope remains candidate input for Phase 1 → Phase 2 → Phase 3
(including mandatory contradiction review) → Phase 4.

## Do not emit when

- the PR is still open;
- the merge is planning-only or does not satisfy an approved slice acceptance bar;
- the implementation boundary was not already approved or approval state is ambiguous;
- harvest / triage with no approved implementation merge;
- unowned read-only review/docs work.

## After approved implementation merge (phase B)

Write the payload in phase B closeout only (not a post-merge slice-doc edit on `main`): approved issue
IDs; slice **Done** only when the full approved child boundary shipped; parent truthful current status
(or **do not change**) unless full parent completion is independently proven; verbatim lifecycle/evidence
comment (PR URL + what shipped + validation); candidate-evidence reference if any; **Do not** list;
already-posted flag.

## Local agent

Verify approval basis, then apply the lifecycle/evidence payload verbatim. Preserve truthful parent state,
skip duplicates with the same PR URL and facts, and never convert candidate evidence into backlog scope.
